Additional notes about formatting floppies (recorded for posterity):

+ 1.  After ready asserts after seek, must wait 300 ms before format.
+ 2.  After seek, should wait 150 usec. before checking for ready or
      else could see prior ready before the line gets deasserted. (< 1 msec)
      AIEE.  One spec suggests more like 150 msec!
+ 3.  After mode change, wait 600 msec.
+ 4.  After head change, wait 100 microseconds (0.1 msec)
+ 5.  MFM Format mode doesn't set write intr.  (Was really trying GCR)
+ 6.  GCR Format mode doesn't set write intr.
+ 7.  MFM Format mode gives 128 in error flags, returns -72 (bad data mark
      checksum).  Error actually means CRC error on data field.
+ 7.  Format mode only sends DMA done interrupt, not an interrupt from
      SWIM itself.  (Turns out that code was using virtual address because
      the old X server version of this code passed virtual addresses to
      StartDMA, while our code base uses physical addresses.  Doh!)
+ 8.  Chip appears lobotomized afterwards, with all registers zeroed.
      (I accidentally used the dma vaddr instead of the chip vaddr
      as the base address in the PrintRegs() function.  Oops.)
+ 9.  Verify SetDBDMAPhysicalAddress (is different in X Server version, 
      including changes to when interrupts are generated.)
+10.  floppycore.c:2185 - 600 msec delay should not happen when polling for
      media presence....  :-)

